====================================================================================================
THE PREDICTION THAT IS NOT YET MEASURED
====================================================================================================
  a0 = c H_Lam / (2 pi) = c H0 sqrt(Omega_L) / (2 pi)
     = (8.6257 +/- 0.0830) e-11 m/s^2        [Planck inputs only, 0.96 %]
  equivalently  a0 / (c H0) = sqrt(Omega_L)/(2 pi) = 0.131724  (no free parameter)
  equivalently  a0 / (c H_Lam) = 1/(2 pi) = 0.159155 exactly

  discriminating tests, in order of how soon they bite:
   (1) a0 to 4.3 %% separates the lock from the record's fitted kappa = 1/2 (8.5 %% apart).
       Current combined a0 error 22.7 %%; CFG493's route floor 8.9 %%; its power label 'NOT POSSIBLE'.
   (2) a0 to ~5 %% separates the vacuum lock (H_Lam) from the total-rate lock (H_0), which are
       20.8 %% apart (0.4607 vs 0.5567).  NOT separable today (pulls 0.44 vs 1.27).
   (3) if dark energy is dynamical: the lock tracks rho_DE(z), not rho_Lam(0), so
       a0(z)/a0(0) = sqrt(rho_DE(z)/rho_DE(0)) = (1+z)^{1.5(1+w)} for constant w.
       w = -1: flat (0.000 dex at every z, the framework's flat law).
       DESI DR2 w0wa at face value: -0.057 dex at z=0.9 (L276's DESI column), vs +0.25 dex for
       the H(z) law and 0.000 for flat.  L276 grades this arm UNDECIDED: no measurement exists.
   (4) the lock is a PHASE TRANSITION, so the rate Q is pinned, not smoothed: it predicts a
       universal non-analyticity at g = a0 (a kink in Q, hence in the RAR) rather than the
       analytic crossover mu = u/(1+u).  The width/shape of the RAR at g = a0 is not measured.

